# Autonomy policy (managed by pstack-kit)

This rule narrows pstack's poteto-mode Autonomy section. Where they differ, this rule wins, including under "don't stop", "going to bed" or any full-autonomy grant.

## Agents do without asking

- Read anything in the repo, git history, Linear, Notion and Slack.
- Create branches, commit, push their own branches, and open or update pull requests ready for review.
- Run local commands: install, typecheck, lint, test, `wrangler dev --local`, the verification skill, `wrangler d1|kv|r2 ... --local`.
- Comment on their own PRs and Linear issues they are working.

## Always pause for a human

Stop, say exactly what you would run and why, and wait. Never route around the pause with a different command, an MCP tool, the Cloudflare API, or a script.

| Action | Examples | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Merge any PR | `gh pr merge`, `--auto`, `origin pr merge`, approving a PR | A human merges every PR. |
| Deploy or change traffic | `wrangler deploy`, `wrangler versions deploy`, `wrangler rollback`, `wrangler triggers deploy`, `wrangler pages deploy` | Production changes are human-owned. |
| Secrets | `wrangler secret put/delete/bulk`, `wrangler versions secret`, editing GitHub or Cloudflare secrets | Agents never hold or change secrets. |
| Remote data | any `wrangler ... --remote`, `wrangler d1 create/delete/export/time-travel`, D1/KV/R2 writes through the Cloudflare MCP or API | Remote D1, KV and R2 are real data. |
| Production DNS and routes | Cloudflare DNS API, `dns_records`, zone settings, `terraform apply` | DNS mistakes are outages. |
| History on shared branches | force-push to `main` or another person's branch, pushing directly to `main` | Shared history is irreversible for others. |
| Customer-visible messages | posting in client Slack channels, emailing customers | Reputational and irreversible. |

`.cursor/hooks/pstack-kit-guard.mjs` blocks the shell forms of these. Cloud agent environments hold no production token, so the API forms fail too. Both are backstops. This rule is the policy.

## Before opening a PR

- Run the verification skill (`.cursor/skills/verify-*/`) for the behavior you changed and paste the evidence into the PR template.
- Keep the diff under the limit in `.pstack-kit/config.json` (400 changed lines by default). Split larger work into stacked PRs, each with its own evidence.
- Multi-PR work gets a plan in `docs/plans/active/` first. See `docs/plans/README.md`.
